{"kind":"request","text":"C1 needs a ruling on two remaining owner acts from sales design section7 before I encode their outcome semantics. Request7a7d976c and promise0fff5d0c remain active. The slot sequence and admitted-post log follow rulings4ea1e06e,8bd8f96c,e7152200; source preparation is unvalidated.\n\nFor record-posting, the design permits an owner to post manually and record a link. Terminal requestOutcome values belong only to native publish result clauses, and the seven post states have no manual-posted state. I propose an owner-signed report with separate manual text/link/actor/fact fields, no invented destination admission, and no change to requestOutcome. Should its slot become done from this explicit member report, or stay overdue until a native admission? The latter would keep a completed manual-channel post in the owner's late carousel forever.\n\nFor retire, the design requires two independent publish-file sends: a short notice over the post file, and a rewritten index. A post becomes final when retired, so further owner transitions cannot repair a refused retirement. I propose recording the owner's retirement intent as retired immediately, preserving any earlier admitted requestOutcome/admittedAt for the log, and retaining each notice/index result separately in native entries. If either write refuses, the log must not say the retirement publication succeeded. Is this sufficient for C1, or should a live separate retirement item own both outcomes and retry before the post reaches final retired? That extra item uses current forms but is a design choice. I have not implemented either act. Please rule on the smallest truthful sequence within current forms. No shared source, live room or deployment changes are requested.","body":{"conditions":"Rule on the manual-posting slot outcome and the smallest truthful two-publication retirement sequence within current forms.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}